# NO trailing slash, and that is the whole point of this line. `node_modules/`
# matches a DIRECTORY only, so it did not match the tracked `node_modules`
# SYMLINK (mode 120000) pointing at $HOME/mcp/backbencher-brain/node_modules
# -- a path that does not exist. A dangling symlink that the ignore rule cannot see
# is a permanent ` D node_modules` in `git status`, which means any `git add -A`
# or `git commit -a` in this repo commits the DELETION of node_modules for everyone
# who checks it out, and every probe, gate and typecheck that shells out to
# ./node_modules/.bin fails on a fresh clone. A pattern without the trailing slash
# matches both the directory and the symlink, so neither can be tracked again.
node_modules
dist/
*.tgz
bun.lock
bb-ts-core.wasm
.bb-data/
bb.json
.bb_backups/

# Local secrets (never commit)
.env.local
.env*.local

# website/ (absorbed from a nested repo) — mirror its local ignores
website/.next/
website/.vercel/
website/.astro/
website/*.log
website/*.tsbuildinfo
website/.env.vercel

# VSIX build artifacts (packaging evidence records the artifact, not the blob)
*.vsix
.p3-runner.tmp.ts
tool-mode-corpus.json.fresh
.tools/

# @vscode/test-electron download cache (R3/M25 e2e artifacts)
.vscode-test/

# M55.V1 rig's isolated VS Code profile: a LOCAL 74 MB install artifact (the
# fresh-VSIX install under test). The frames and the session manifest are the
# evidence and ARE committed; this profile is machine-local and never is.
validation/m55/profile/

# client-tooling client runtime dir
.client-tooling/

# tree-sitter grammar build outputs. `tree-sitter generate` writes a ~16MB
# parser.c and the node-types/grammar JSON, and `tree-sitter build` writes a
# local wasm; only the hand-written grammar sources (grammar.js, package.json,
# tree-sitter.json, README, scanner.h) are tracked. The wasm the product loads
# is the one committed under wasm/, which is the artifact the evidence names.
# NOTE: the pattern excludes the CONTENTS of src/, not the directory, because
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded -- the
# scanner.c negation below is inert if this reads `src/`.
grammars/tree-sitter-*/src/*
grammars/tree-sitter-*/tree-sitter-*.wasm
# ...EXCEPT hand-written external scanners, which are SOURCE, not build output.
# The set of grammar source files that must be tracked for a rebuild is named in
# the comment above as "grammar.js, package.json, tree-sitter.json, README,
# scanner.h" -- and `scanner.h` covers the headers an in-tree scanner dir holds.
# tree-sitter-cpp's external scanner is `src/scanner.c`, so the blanket `src/`
# ignore silently dropped the one file its grammar cannot be rebuilt without.
# Found while vendoring tree-sitter-cpp for #743: the ignore list named the
# scanner by its C++-in-fsharp-style filename instead of by its role.
!grammars/tree-sitter-cpp/src/scanner.c

# tree-sitter-perl (1.2.1, vendored by the M14.6 perl wave) needs the same three
# roles, plus one more this grammar has: its external scanner at `src/scanner.c`
# includes `tree_sitter/parser.h`, so the header tree is SOURCE here and not
# build output — without it the vendored scanner cannot be compiled and the lane
# has no rebuild path. `src/parser.c` (29 MB, regenerated by
# `tree-sitter generate`) stays ignored, and so do the per-language generated
# scanner headers `tsp_*.h`/`bsearch.h`, which `tree-sitter generate` copies in
# alongside parser.c.
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/grammar.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/scanner.c
# ...and the header DIRECTORY has to be un-ignored before the files inside it
# can be: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded (the
# same trap the note above records for `src/`), so the negation is two levels.
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/parser.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/alloc.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/array.h
# tree-sitter-vbnet (govindbanura/tree-sitter-vbnet, vendored AND heavily
# PATCHED by the M60 VB wave -- 18 repairs, each with a repro case under
# fixtures/grammar-repro/cases) needs the same two generated files as nim and
# hcl, for the same reason: they are what `script/m14/verify-grammar-pins.ts`
# reads to run its offline source<->wasm proof. Without them the pin's check
# reports "not applicable" and the lane has no proof that the committed wasm is a
# build of the committed grammar -- which for a patched grammar is the one claim
# that matters most, since the patches live in `grammar.js`.
# `src/parser.c` (29 MB, regenerated by `tree-sitter generate`) stays ignored,
# the same call made for perl: unlike graphql's 283 KB, 29 MB is not something to
# put in git for hermeticity. The rebuild path is
# `tree-sitter generate && tree-sitter build --wasm`, and the two JSON files are
# the digest-stable evidence that a regeneration changed nothing that matters.
!grammars/tree-sitter-vbnet/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-vbnet/src/grammar.json
# tree-sitter-xml (tree-sitter-grammars 0.7.0 @ 5000ae8f, vendored AND PATCHED
# by the M60 xml lane) needs the same roles graphql took, plus ONE this grammar
# uniquely has: its external scanner is a HEADER, `common/scanner.h`, shared by
# both the `xml` and `dtd` grammars and included by `xml/src/scanner.c`. That
# makes `common/scanner.h` SOURCE, not build output — and it is the file the M60
# repair edits (`skip_if_eq` in `scan_pi_content`), so if it went untracked the
# repair would be invisible in the diff and unrebuildable from the repository.
# The layout is upstream's (`<lang>/` per grammar, `common/` shared), so the
# patterns are nested one level deeper than the flat grammars.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/common/scanner.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/common/common.mjs
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/grammar.json
# ...and `xml/src/parser.c` too: 254 KB, the same call hcl (600 KB) and graphql
# (283 KB) made. With it tracked, the wired wasm is rebuildable from TRACKED files
# alone, so `measureVendored`'s per-file digests do not move on a `tree-sitter
# generate` that changed nothing else.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/parser.c
# ...and `xml/src/scanner.c`, which `#include`s the shared header above and is
# therefore equally required for a rebuild.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/scanner.c
# tree-sitter-hcl (tree-sitter-grammars 1.2.0 @ 64ad6278, vendored for the M60
# HCL lane): the grammar-pin instrument's offline source↔wasm proof needs the
# two GENERATED files (`script/m14/verify-grammar-pins.ts` `sourceVsWasmFor`),
# and without them the pin would record a sha with no proof that the wired bytes
# are a build of the committed source — which is the whole property the pin buys
# over an unversioned blob.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/grammar.json
# ...and the two files the wasm is REBUILT from. Unlike haskell (20 MB) and
# elixir (13 MB) this parser is 600 KB, so it is kept: the pin then rebuilds
# offline rather than resting on a hash alone.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/parser.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/scanner.c
# ...and the tree-sitter headers `parser.c` includes, without which a rebuild
# fails at the preprocessor rather than at the grammar.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/tree_sitter/

# tree-sitter-graphql (bkegley 0.0.1 @ ee5ce96, vendored AND PATCHED by the
# M12.38/177 graphql wave) needs the same two generated files, plus two roles
# this grammar has and no other one does: the port script `port.py`, which is
# SOURCE here because `grammar.js` is GENERATED by it from `grammar.upstream.js`
# — the two together are the reviewable form of the patch, and deleting port.py
# would leave grammar.js un-reproducible — and the pristine upstream file it
# reads, so the port is idempotent and auditable rather than one-shot.
# `src/parser.c` (283 KB, regenerated by `tree-sitter generate`) stays ignored.
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/grammar.json
# ...and `src/parser.c` too, which is the OPPOSITE of nim (41 MB) and perl
# (29 MB) and the SAME call hcl made (600 KB): at 283 KB it is small enough to
# keep, and keeping it is what makes this lane's pin hermetic. `measureVendored`
# hashes every file in the tree, tracked or not, so an UNTRACKED parser.c would
# make the gate go red after any `tree-sitter generate` — which is exactly the
# drift the nim lane is reporting right now for its own src/grammar.json. With
# parser.c tracked, the wired wasm is rebuildable from TRACKED files alone and
# the recorded digests do not move on a regeneration that changed nothing else.
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/parser.c
# ...and the three headers `src/parser.c` includes. The pin's `measureVendored`
# hashes EVERY file in the vendored tree, tracked or not, and records 13. If the
# headers stay untracked, a fresh clone has 10, hashes to a different tree
# digest, and the lane's own pin gate goes RED on a clean checkout — the
# hermeticity argument above, applied one level down. `src/parser.c` is
# `#include "tree_sitter/parser.h"`, so the committed parser.c is not even
# compilable without the committed parser.h: the tracked set was internally
# inconsistent, and only a fresh-clone check would have shown it.
# The DIRECTORY has to be re-included before its contents can be: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so negating the three headers alone is
# silently a no-op (it tracked 10 files, not 13, and reported no error).
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/tree_sitter/
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/tree_sitter/parser.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/tree_sitter/alloc.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-graphql/src/tree_sitter/array.h

# M60 Make wave (2026-09-27). tree-sitter-make vendors `src/parser.c` (928 KB)
# and the same hermeticity argument as the lanes above applies with EXTRA force
# here: this lane's central claim IS the source<->wasm identity proof, and that
# proof is not checkable without the generated source. `src/parser.c` is
# `#include "tree_sitter/parser.h"`, so committing parser.c without the headers
# leaves the tracked set internally inconsistent — a fresh clone would not build
# it and the pin could not be re-derived. The DIRECTORY must be re-included
# before its contents can be: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so
# negating the headers alone is silently a no-op.
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/grammar.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/parser.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/tree_sitter/
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/tree_sitter/parser.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/tree_sitter/alloc.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-make/src/tree_sitter/array.h
# tree-sitter-proto (amaanq/tree-sitter-proto @ e9f6b43, vendored AND PATCHED by
# the protobuf lane) needs the same three roles graphql took, and for the same
# reasons stated there: the two GENERATED JSONs, because `sourceVsWasmFor` needs
# the pair to run the offline source<->wasm proof and without them the check
# reports "not applicable" and the lane has no such proof at all; `src/parser.c`
# because `measureVendored` hashes EVERY file in the tree, tracked or not, so an
# untracked parser.c would turn the gate red after any `tree-sitter generate` —
# 299 KB here, the same call graphql made at 283 KB and hcl at 600 KB, and the
# opposite of nim at 41 MB. The DIRECTORY has to be re-included before its
# contents can be: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so negating
# the files alone is silently a no-op (it tracked 0 of them and reported no
# error). tree-sitter.json is NOT ignored and is tracked — upstream has none, and
# without it the CLI falls back to ABI 14 and `tree-sitter build --wasm` refuses.
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/grammar.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/parser.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/tree_sitter/
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/tree_sitter/parser.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/tree_sitter/alloc.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-proto/src/tree_sitter/array.h

# `libxslt/` is a 2,245-file git clone with its OWN `.git`, checked out as a
# dependency. Nothing ignored it, which put it one `git add -A` away from
# committing an entire dependency history as ordinary files — in a repo where
# `node_modules` is a tracked SYMLINK and one mistaken add has already caused
# real damage (see the `node_modules` comment above). A checkout is not source.
libxslt/

# `*.tmp-*` is a crashed or killed run's partial output: `M14.0.F8.json.tmp-2831056`
# was 0 bytes. Same killed-run failure mode the Lua mutation harness just grew a
# sidecar for, in a place with no sidecar to repair from.
*.tmp-*
# — the C lane's generated pair, and the reason it is tracked is hermeticity
# rather than size. `measureVendored` hashes EVERY file in the vendored tree,
# tracked or not, and the pin's source↔wasm proof runs on exactly these two JSONs.
# Before they existed the C lane had NO offline proof that its wired bytes were a
# build of its own source: `sourceVsWasmFor` reported "not applicable", and the
# vendored tree held only grammar.js/LICENSE/package.json/tree-sitter.json.
# `src/parser.c` (3.9 MB, rebuilt by `tree-sitter generate` from grammar.js) and
# `src/tree_sitter/` stay ignored, so the tracked set is exactly the 6 files the
# gate hashes and the recorded digest does not move on a regeneration.
!grammars/tree-sitter-c/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-c/src/grammar.json

# --- carried forward from the m60 grammar-governance line: three entries the other
# laptop's wave had not reached. Same trap, same reason: each is SOURCE, not build
# output. `css/src/scanner.c` carries DESCENDANT_OP / PSEUDO_CLASS_SELECTOR_COLON /
# ERROR_RECOVERY; `html/src/tag.h` is the 126-entry tag table the scanner looks names
# up in, so it decides whether <LINK> is a void element at all. Without them the
!grammars/tree-sitter-css/src/scanner.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-html/src/scanner.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-html/src/tag.h
